## Changes in this package

- Package identity: `dsh-chrome-suite`, plugin row `chrome-suite`, settings route
  `/dsh-chrome-suite/panel`, locale namespace `dsh-chrome-suite`.
- Adds a `browser_status` diagnostic tool that reports host/extension state without reading pages.
- Adds a configurable action allowlist (`allowedActions`, also reads
  `DSH_CHROME_USE_ALLOWED_ACTIONS`) enforced before every tool executes.
- Replaces the settings card's dynamic import of DSH client UI primitives with self-contained
  controls, and marks a stale status when polling fails instead of showing an old "connected".
- Renames the bundled Chrome extension's display name to "Chrome Suite Bridge" (version 1.15.5) so it
  is distinguishable from other installed copies, and adds an in-panel privacy notice.
- Gives the package its own transport identity: host name `com.chromesuite.bridge`, install locations
  `~/.dsh/chrome-suite-bridge` and `~/chrome-suite-bridge-extension`, socket/token/log files under
  `/tmp/chrome-suite-bridge-<uid>/`, and a manifest `key` generated for this package. No other
  extension ID is allowed to reach this host.
- Removes the upstream "nudge the legacy host" path, which would have sent a reload to another
  installed host.
- Host names must match Chrome's grammar `[a-z0-9_]+(\.[a-z0-9_]+)*`: hyphens are rejected with
  "Invalid native messaging host name specified", hence `com.chromesuite.bridge`.
- Fixes the 1.2.0 bug where every tool failed with `undefined` reading `has` because the action
  allowlist was not passed to the check.
- Resolves an omitted `tab` to a tab in the DSH work window when this session has not used one yet,
  so the plugin tools and the `cb` CLI share a default target.
- Adds `browser_find`, `browser_scrape`, `browser_assert` and `browser_wait_response`, all built on the
  existing `eval`/`network` operations, for a tool set of 17.
- Adds records control: a popup button that clears the activity ledger, session ledger and log, a
  "record action details" switch that drops hints, tab titles and error text, and 24-hour caps on
  both the activity ledger and the log. Both controls are reachable only from the toolbar popup. The
  bulk-release button is renamed to "release all tabs" and explains why it is disabled while no tab
  is attached.

## Not changed

- The CDP operation set, the native-messaging wire protocol, and the in-page cursor behaviour.

Because the transport identity is separate, installing this package does not overwrite another
installation, and the extension IDs are distinct. Running two `browser_*` plugins at the same time is
still not recommended: each attaches a debugger to the same Chrome tabs and registers overlapping
tool names.

